docs/reviews/2026-11-18-whole-range/kickoff-fix-f5.md:39:- **Midnight ET and the year boundary:** the new runs at 00:00 to 00:45 read the NEW date's pick, as every run reads `now`'s date: a pick whose first pitch is after midnight on the slate's own evening is not checked after midnight (no regular-season game starts then; stated limit). On January 1 there is no pick. **The clock changes now fall inside the line's hours** (F1b's standing row said the repeated and skipped hours were outside `10-23`; that is no longer true): on the November change cron can run the 01:00 to 01:45 slots twice and on the March change it skips the 02:00 hour. Every such run is outside any entry window and returns before a request; the contract check confirms what Debian cron does and that the interval between two runs can never fall under 870 seconds in a way that matters (a run outside the window holds the lock for well under a second).
